{"path":"cargo/guide/creating-a-new-project.html","title":"Creating a New Package","description":"To start a new package with Cargo, use cargo new:","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":"creating-a-new-package","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creating a New Package"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To start a new "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/appendix/glossary.html#package","title":"\"package\" (glossary entry)","children":[{"type":"text","value":"package"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with Cargo, use "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo new"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ cargo new hello_world --bin"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"We’re passing "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"--bin"},{"type":"text","value":" because we’re making a binary program: if we were making a library, we’d pass "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"--lib"},{"type":"text","value":". This also initializes a new "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"git"},{"type":"text","value":" repository by default. If you don’t want it to do that, pass "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"--vcs none"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Let’s check out what Cargo has generated for us:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ cd hello_world\n$ tree .\n.\n├── Cargo.toml\n└── src\n    └── main.rs\n\n1 directory, 2 files"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Let’s take a closer look at "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.toml"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"[package]\nname = \"hello_world\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[dependencies]"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is called a "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/appendix/glossary.html#manifest","title":"\"manifest\" (glossary entry)","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"manifest"}]}]}]},{"type":"text","value":", and it contains all of the metadata that Cargo needs to compile your package. This file is written in the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://toml.io/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"TOML"}]},{"type":"text","value":" format (pronounced /tɑməl/)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here’s what’s in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"src/main.rs"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"rust","code":"fn main() {\n    println!(\"Hello, world!\");\n}"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cargo generated a “hello world” program for you, otherwise known as a "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/appendix/glossary.html#crate","title":"\"crate\" (glossary entry)","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"binary crate"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":". Let’s compile it:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ cargo build\n   Compiling hello_world v0.1.0 (file:///path/to/package/hello_world)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"And then run it:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ ./target/debug/hello_world\nHello, world!"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also use "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo run"},{"type":"text","value":" to compile and then run it, all in one step (You won’t see the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Compiling"},{"type":"text","value":" line if you have not made any changes since you last compiled):"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ cargo run\n   Compiling hello_world v0.1.0 (file:///path/to/package/hello_world)\n     Running `target/debug/hello_world`\nHello, world!"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You’ll now notice a new file, "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cargo.lock"},{"type":"text","value":". It contains information about your dependencies. Since there are none yet, it’s not very interesting."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Once you’re ready for release, you can use "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo build --release"},{"type":"text","value":" to compile your files with optimizations turned on:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"bash","code":"$ cargo build --release\n   Compiling hello_world v0.1.0 (file:///path/to/package/hello_world)"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo build --release"},{"type":"text","value":" puts the resulting binary in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"target/release"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"target/debug"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compiling in debug mode is the default for development. Compilation time is shorter since the compiler doesn’t do optimizations, but the code will run slower. Release mode takes longer to compile, but the code will run faster."}]}]}}
